SUMM = {
    "2611.09822": {
        "zh": "量子算法的突破依赖算法创新，但量子程序只能在受限或小规模实例上由经典计算机验证，自动搜索难以扩展。作者在 Lean 中建立量子程序库，令 LLM 智能体按形式化规格合成新程序，并由定理证明器检验其正确性与代价；智能体以团队方式协作，通过 wiki 共享结果与知识、开会讨论思路。结果在并行搜索上取得最高 1.4 倍、量子算术 290 倍、聚变/光化学/药物代谢相关模拟 11/8/2.5 倍的改进，且这些程序已超出当今经典与量子计算机的可测范围。",
        "en": "Quantum algorithm progress is bottlenecked by the fact that quantum programs can only be checked on restricted or small instances. The authors build a quantum program library inside Lean in which LLM agents synthesize programs against formal specifications and the proof assistant verifies both correctness and cost; agent teams collaborate through wikis and organised conferences. They report order-of-magnitude improvements on scientific applications—up to 1.4x on parallel search, 290x on quantum arithmetic, and 11x, 8x and 2.5x on simulations relevant to fusion, photochemistry and drug metabolism—for programs that today's classical and quantum computers cannot test.",
    },
    "2611.09410": {
        "zh": "主流共享内存语言靠锁等同步机制隔离共享访问，但同步只约束时间顺序，普通读写仍在时刻通信，程序员须自行理解「顺序—通信」关系才能正确隔离。作者提出 Sync-as-Share 内存模型：以线程隔离为起点，每个线程读写私有视图，把程序中既有的同步动作重新解释为显式通信，凡不在同步点就不通信，从而按构造排除数据竞争，冲突在同步点检测。作者给出两种通信拓扑以权衡取舍，并在 Java 上实例化为「版本控制内存」（同步动作在私有视图间推拉更新），在 Rocq 中机器检验，证明在 Java 内存模型下正确同步的程序在两种语义下行为一致。",
        "en": "Synchronisation in shared-memory languages enforces only temporal ordering while ordinary reads and writes still communicate, so isolation depends on programmers correctly understanding the ordering/communication relationship. Sync-as-Share instead starts from thread isolation—each thread reads and writes a private view—and reinterprets existing synchronisation actions as explicit communication, so nothing is communicated outside synchronisation actions and data races become impossible by construction, with conflicting updates detected at synchronisation points. Two communication topologies with different trade-offs are proposed; the Java instantiation treats the memory model's own synchronisation actions as the only communication points, is formalised as version-controlled memory and mechanised in Rocq, and is proved to preserve the behaviour of correctly synchronised Java programs.",
    },
    "2611.09307": {
        "zh": "智能合约模糊测试器在吞吐上相差一个数量级，在输入构造设计上也各不相同，而已有对比很少把两者分开。Wake 5 是开源 Python 框架，以内嵌 EVM（revm）取代外部节点的 JSON-RPC，并通过 MCP 服务器把静态分析暴露给语言模型智能体。在 Daedaluzz 迷宫基准（153 条可达断言、守卫常量小于 2^32）上，Wake 5 每秒执行 29,931 笔交易，与 Foundry 持平、比 Echidna 快 11.5 倍；但八小时跑下来三者中位数只到 75/71/70 条断言，并集 93 条——说明浅层断言耗尽后，瓶颈是输入生成器的先验而非吞吐。由 LLM 智能体编写、用约束求解器生成输入的 harness，在五次运行中每次 33–79 分钟内命中全部 153 条断言。",
        "en": "Smart-contract fuzzers differ by an order of magnitude in throughput and by design in input construction, yet published comparisons rarely separate the two. Wake 5 is an open-source Python framework that replaces JSON-RPC to an external node with an in-process EVM (revm) and exposes static analysis to LLM agents through an MCP server. On the Daedaluzz maze benchmark it executes 29,931 transactions per second, on par with Foundry and 11.5x faster than Echidna, yet in eight-hour campaigns all three plateau at medians of 75, 71 and 70 assertions (union 93): once shallow assertions are exhausted, the generator prior rather than throughput is the binding constraint. A harness written by an LLM agent using a constraint solver reached all 153 assertions in five campaigns, in 33 to 79 minutes each.",
    },
    "2611.09008": {
        "zh": "专家并行 MoE 层按最忙 GPU 的节奏推进，少数热点专家承担了大部分超载。若在每层复制热点专家即可均衡负载，前提是权重能在层内到达，而从属主广播正是瓶颈：点对点复制把属主压垮，基线广播则付出延迟或带宽开销。ISER-MoE 在 TensorRT-LLM 中实现，通过 NVLink 交换机把热点专家组播到固定 GPU 组，使每个字节只离开属主一次；GPU 调度器逐层分配热点专家到组，多端口广播把注入分摊到组内端口，两者与共享专家重叠执行。轨迹回放中调度器消除 98–99% 的超载；DeepSeek-V4-Pro 预填充服务在数学基准上吞吐提升 17.4%、智能体提示上 7.2%。",
        "en": "Expert-parallel MoE layers advance at the pace of the most loaded GPU, and a few hot experts carry most of the excess load. Replicating them helps only if the weights arrive within the layer, and broadcasting from the owner is the bottleneck. ISER-MoE, built in TensorRT-LLM, multicasts hot experts through the NVLink switch to fixed GPU groups so each byte leaves its owner once, with a per-layer GPU scheduler and multi-port broadcast overlapped with the shared expert. Trace replay shows the scheduler removes 98–99% of the excess load; prefill serving of DeepSeek-V4-Pro gains 17.4% throughput on a math benchmark and 7.2% on agentic prompts.",
    },
    "2611.08864": {
        "zh": "大模型异步强化学习的 rollout 存在三类利用率损失：小批内长度异构造成的填充气泡、长尾输出造成的偏斜气泡、以及按长度排序派发导致的训练队列占用波动（排序气泡）。ASP 用一次离线预处理同时削减三者：把各实例的请求按长度与产出分布重排，使多实例 rollout 既突破单实例推理的早期扩展平台、又让样本到达训练器的节奏更平滑。调度器嵌入把 rollout 与训练解耦、同时保持策略滞后可观测且有界的异步架构。端到端吞吐最高提升 3.22 倍，迭代时间比 MindSpeed-RL 降低最多 76.8%、比 verl 降低最多 62.5%；调度本身贡献 10.9% 的迭代时间下降。已用于内部电信域 RL 后训练，训练周期由三个多月缩短到约两个月。",
        "en": "ASP is an offline rollout scheduler for multi-instance asynchronous RL of LLMs that removes three sources of rollout underutilization in a single preprocessing pass: padding bubbles from intra-minibatch length heterogeneity, skewness bubbles from long-tail outputs, and sorting bubbles from training-queue fluctuations induced by length-sorted dispatch. It is integrated into an asynchronous architecture that decouples rollout from training while keeping policy lag observable and bounded. It improves end-to-end throughput by up to 3.22x, reduces iteration time by up to 76.8% versus MindSpeed-RL and 62.5% versus verl (scheduling alone accounts for 10.9%), scales more robustly with more generation resources, and reduced an internal telecom RL post-training period from over three months to about two.",
    },
    "2611.09065": {
        "zh": "LLM 智能体已能自行生成查询并在真实数据上执行，但「查询是否合法」「最终答案是否正确」两项检查都无法判断智能体是否在运行前就知道查询会产生什么结果。作者提出必须单独评测这种「后果预测」能力，并构建 MongoBench：给定文档集合与 find() 过滤条件，模型须返回精确匹配的 _id 集合，真值由真实 mongod 产生。300 道题各由三四个有文档记载的匹配陷阱组合而成，且由三家厂商的模型对称出题。四个模型准确率 70.1%–92.1%（跨度 22 点），每个出题模型对自己出的题也误判 10%–31%，说明「能写出查询」不等于「能预测其效果」。错误更好地由查询触发的语义陷阱（范围比较、null）而非文档数等表层指标预测；附上经核验的规则表收益不均；交由引擎执行可获得可靠匹配集，但对 28% 的题需核查委派是否忠实。",
        "en": "MongoBench argues that an agent's ability to predict what its query will do must be evaluated in its own right, separately from query validity and final-answer correctness. Given a document collection and a MongoDB find() filter, a model must return the exact set of matching _ids, with ground truth from a real mongod. Each of the 300 items composes three or four documented matching pitfalls and is proposed symmetrically by three vendors' models. Accuracy ranges from 70.1% to 92.1% across four models, and each proposer mispredicts 10–31% of the items it wrote itself, so producing a query does not imply predicting its effect. Errors are better predicted by which semantic pitfall (range comparison, null) a query exercises than by surface measures, and delegating execution to the engine works but must be checked.",
    },
    "2611.09159": {
        "zh": "边缘应用日益同时包含 CNN 感知与可在边缘部署的 Transformer 语言模型，而推理延迟既随输入难度变化、也随运行时硬件状态变化，使异构负载难以部署。提前退出可降低计算，但现有方法往往绑定具体模型，且依赖在动态边缘环境下会过期的静态延迟画像。UniExit 把 CNN 块与 Transformer 层统一抽象为有序阶段，套用同一套延迟感知路由策略、同时保留各模型特有的质量控制；它依据运行时状态与推理进度预测「到达下一个出口」的代价，做预算感知的继续/退出决策，并组合缓存复用、趋势回退与 CNN 专用的退出稳定化以降低开销。在多类边缘与边云平台上，无论单负载、并发异构还是边云场景，均优于既有的渐进推理基线，同时减少冗余出口计算与任务级能耗。",
        "en": "UniExit is a unified latency-aware early-exit runtime for heterogeneous edge AI that abstracts CNN blocks and Transformer layers as ordered stages and applies one latency-aware routing policy while keeping model-specific quality mechanisms. It predicts the cost of reaching the next exit from runtime state and inference progress to make budget-aware continue-or-exit decisions, combining runtime-state-aware latency prediction, cache-based reuse, trend-aware fallback and CNN-specific exit stabilisation. Across single-workload, concurrent heterogeneous and edge-cloud settings it improves deadline satisfaction and latency-accuracy trade-offs over progressive-inference baselines while reducing redundant exit computation and task-level energy.",
    },
    "2611.08697": {
        "zh": "中小企业和个人用户出于成本与数据隐私考虑倾向在本地跑智能体，这使边缘 CPU 的性能特征成为体验瓶颈，但此前缺乏系统刻画。作者在 Intel 边缘 CPU 上用 TerminalBench 做八组实验，考察核心频率、非核心（uncore）频率、活跃物理核数与超线程对智能体任务 CPU 侧延迟的影响。结论：P 核频率的影响最大，从 2.5 GHz 提到 5.5 GHz，单智能体加速 1.154 倍、八个并发智能体加速 1.341 倍；其余参数影响有限。作者同时开源可复现的 CPU 侧延迟评测框架与数据集，并称是首个在单/多智能体配置下刻画硬件微架构关系的工作。",
        "en": "A study of how CPU micro-architectural characteristics affect CPU-side latency of agentic AI, motivated by local agent deployment for cost and privacy. Across eight experiments on an Intel edge CPU with TerminalBench, P-core frequency produces the largest median latency improvement: raising it from 2.5 to 5.5 GHz yields a 1.154x speedup for a single agent and 1.341x for eight concurrent agents, while uncore frequency, active physical cores and SMT matter far less. The authors release an open framework and dataset for repeatable CPU-side agentic latency benchmarking.",
    },
    "2611.09346": {
        "zh": "大数据架构的可扩展性通常靠纵向或横向扩容解决，但这种以硬件为中心的视角忽略了存储层的「逻辑可扩展性」：当数据模型与查询模式错配时，性能瓶颈会持续性存在，与算力多寡无关。作者用文档型、图型与多模型三种数据库范式，在不同负载、查询与数据规模下做对比实验。结果表明模型错配导致的性能退化无法靠增加机器弥补——在结构上不合适的模型下加机器，性能与单机相当甚至更差，因为分布式协调开销会放大逻辑模型的低效。效率最大化的条件是数据库逻辑结构与数据本质及分析范围相匹配，这一条件比任何基础设施扩容策略都更具决定性。",
        "en": "Big-data scalability is usually pursued through vertical or horizontal scaling, which overlooks the logical scalability of the storage layer. Comparing document, graph and multi-model database paradigms under varying workloads, queries and dataset scales, the paper shows that performance degradation caused by model misalignment cannot be mitigated by adding computational resources: increasing machines while keeping a structurally inadequate data model yields performance equivalent to or worse than a single-machine configuration, because distributed coordination overhead compounds the inefficiencies of the logical model. Efficiency is maximised when the logical structure matches the nature of the data and the intended analysis scope—a condition more decisive than any infrastructural scaling strategy.",
    },
    "2611.09207": {
        "zh": "强化学习已成为训练推理语言模型的核心，但每个 RL step 都要耦合多个大模型、异构阶段、跨步状态与复杂异步依赖，使流水线既难扩展又昂贵，而现有系统只优化设计空间的一部分。作者提出以数据为中心的图中间表示 RPEG，把流水线结构与执行联合优化：结构侧暴露有界异步、actor-critic 共享等选择，执行侧暴露阶段融合、细粒度调度与多维模型并行；并配套一个覆盖计算、通信、内存与机架/节点/GPU 层次效应的分析性能模型。在最多 256 张 GH200 上，实现 RPEG 的分布式运行时比 ReaL 快最多 2 倍、比 verl 降低最多 2.48 倍步延迟，硬件利用率提升最多 30%。",
        "en": "RPEG is a data-centric graph intermediate representation that jointly optimises the structure and execution of reinforcement-learning pipelines for reasoning language models, which otherwise couple multiple large models, heterogeneous stages, cross-step state and asynchronous dependencies. The graph exposes structural choices such as bounded asynchrony and actor-critic sharing alongside execution optimisations including stage fusion, fine-grained scheduling and multi-dimensional model parallelism, backed by an analytical performance model covering compute, communication, memory and rack/node/GPU-level effects. On up to 256 GH200 GPUs the runtime improves performance by up to 2x over ReaL, cuts step latency by up to 2.48x versus verl, and raises hardware utilisation by up to 30%.",
    },
    "2611.09161": {
        "zh": "智能体已进入编码、银行、电商等场景，因能调用工具、改变应用状态，安全测试成为可靠部署的前提，但基于真实生产环境的基准仍然稀缺。GreyZone 用于评测自动化红队服务：与 AgentDojo 等主要评测「被攻击的智能体」不同，它评测服务「生成并投递能造成经验证的安全策略违规的攻击」的能力。作者挑选独立开发、带访问权限/机密性/行为授权边界的开源智能体应用，攻击面覆盖多智能体交互与多模态输入，并在保留生产相关工作流的真实环境中独立核验结果。文中给出用 Promptfoo 在 Letta Code 与 Clawith 上的两个初步案例，公开基准（含被测智能体与各应用攻击面）以支持后续研究。",
        "en": "GreyZone is a benchmark for evaluating automated red-teaming services against real-world agent applications. Unlike benchmarks such as AgentDojo, which evaluate subject agents under attack, it evaluates a service's ability to generate and deliver attacks that cause verified security-policy violations. Subject applications are independently developed open-source agents with access-permission, confidentiality and action-authorisation boundaries, exposing attack surfaces from multi-agent interaction and multimodal input, and outcomes are independently verified in environments that preserve production-relevant workflows. Two preliminary case studies with Promptfoo on Letta Code and Clawith examine attack delivery, agent behaviour and verified outcomes.",
    },
    "2611.09802": {
        "zh": "Claude Code 等编码智能体每次会话都读仓库的指令文件（AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md），这类文件会像所有文档一样落后于代码而「过期」，构成技术债中的文档债，其「利息」是之后每次会话都要付的额外代价。只检查任务是否成功的评测看不到这笔成本，过期文件因而长期留存。作者从三个活跃开源仓库取三类真实过期指令（测试命令、代码位置、添加组件的步骤），在「保持过期 / 修正为当前路径 / 删除」三个版本下让智能体完成 22 个维护任务，代码与任务固定，分析两个模型共 732 条轨迹的逐次工具调用。发现：指令与任务相关时智能体会遵循过期内容，甚至在其他地方已有正确信息时亦然；过期测试命令使 Claude Sonnet 5.5 每次多花约两次工具调用（多三分之一）；其余场景差异不可检出；智能体虽能从即时失败中恢复，但无一修复底层指令文件；修正指令可消除对废弃路径的操作，删除则可阻止大多数。",
        "en": "Coding agents read repository instruction files such as AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md every session, and these can fall behind the code, becoming documentation debt whose interest is paid in every later session. Using three real stale instructions from active open-source repositories—a test command, a code location, and a procedure—the authors have agents perform 22 maintenance tasks under three versions of each instruction (stale, corrected, removed) with code and task held fixed, analysing 732 trajectories of two models at the level of individual tool calls. Agents follow stale guidance when it is relevant, sometimes even when correct information is available; the stale test command cost Claude Sonnet 5.5 about two extra tool calls per run; agents recovered from immediate failures but none repaired the instruction file, while correcting or removing instructions eliminated operations on obsolete paths.",
    },
    "2611.09470": {
        "zh": "智能手机、智能家居中枢与可穿戴设备面临日益复杂的 Android 恶意软件，而集中式检测带来隐私与扩展性顾虑。联邦学习可在不上传原始数据的前提下协同训练，但客户端部分参与、本地模型质量参差会破坏全局优化的稳定性。作者提出 DW-FedADMM：把原始-对偶协调与「依赖表现的客户端加权」结合，动态系数在增广拉格朗日更新前调制各参与客户端的本地状态，对偶变量则约束本地与全局模型状态的分歧。在 Drebin、Malgenome、TUANDROMD 三个基准上，以 5/10/15 个客户端、IID 分片、部分参与、5 与 10 轮通信预算各跑十个随机种子：Drebin 上种子平均准确率最高（97.64%±0.20%），18 个配置中 9 个（含 10 轮预算的 9 个中 7 个）均值最优；总体池化 95.42% 准确率、94.62% F1、96.06% 精确率、99.45% AUC，均略优于 FedADMM，且平均假阳率与客户端更新范数最低。",
        "en": "DW-FedADMM is a federated optimisation framework for distributed Android malware defence that combines primal-dual coordination with performance-dependent client-side weighting: a dynamic coefficient modulates each participating client's local state before the augmented-Lagrangian update, while dual variables regulate disagreement between local and global model states. On Drebin, Malgenome and TUANDROMD with 5, 10 and 15 clients, IID shards, partial participation and 5- or 10-round budgets over ten seeds, it attains the highest seed-averaged accuracy on Drebin (97.64%±0.20%) and the best mean accuracy in 9 of 18 configurations, with pooled 95.42% accuracy, 94.62% F1, 96.06% precision and 99.45% AUC—slightly ahead of FedADMM—and the lowest mean false-positive rate and smallest client update norm among six methods.",
    },
    "2611.09411": {
        "zh": "多模态训练打破了传统流水线「数据加载与模型执行松耦合」的假设：解码代价、token/latent 数量与张量大小的样本级差异，使 CPU 预处理时间与 GPU 计算时间在各数据并行 rank 上大幅波动，且在同步训练中相互纠缠——GPU 执行决定输入流水线有多少时间准备下一批，某个 rank 预处理延迟又会让所有 GPU 在同步点停摆。因此单独优化 CPU 吞吐或 GPU 负载均衡都无法消除气泡。DataHelix 采用「元数据优先」的 CPU-GPU 协同调度：把每个 GPU 计算窗口当作下一批的就绪预算，跨 rank 协调预处理以最小化错期而非 CPU 完工时间；在样本仍是轻量描述符时决定放置，避免昂贵的数据搬运；描述符级 token-latent 感知分批做粗平衡，代价门控的集合重平衡只在其预期收益超过传输开销时纠正残余偏斜。在 8 张昇腾 910B、11 个视频与多模态负载上，平均错期率降低 67.8%、p95 输入等待延迟降低 87.0%，同 CPU 预算下吞吐为 rank 本地 DataLoader 的 2.72 倍几何均值、Ray actor 池的 1.82 倍。",
        "en": "DataHelix is a metadata-first CPU-GPU co-scheduling data plane for multimodal training, where per-sample variation in decoding cost, token/latent count and tensor size makes CPU preprocessing and GPU compute times fluctuate across data-parallel ranks and interact tightly under synchronous training. It treats each GPU compute window as the readiness budget for the next batch and coordinates preprocessing across ranks to minimise deadline misses rather than CPU makespan, deciding placement while samples are still lightweight descriptors, using descriptor-level token-latent-aware batching for coarse balancing and cost-gated collective rebalancing for residual skew. On 8 Ascend 910B accelerators across 11 video and multimodal workloads it reduces mean deadline-miss rate by 67.8% and p95 input-wait latency by 87.0%, with 2.72x geometric-mean throughput over rank-local DataLoaders and 1.82x over a Ray actor pool.",
    },
    "2611.09433": {
        "zh": "离线模仿学习要同时保证高回报与强安全约束，现有做法要么依赖难以为复杂现实约束设计的显式代价函数，要么要求既有安全性又高性能的专家示范，采集成本过高。作者提出双专家模仿学习：一类示范严格遵守安全规范但可能次优，另一类追求高回报但可能违规。方法 DexDICE 把 DICE 式离线学习与安全支撑约束结合，取代常规的分布约束，使智能体能利用高回报行为而不越出安全合规区域；并证明满足该约束的理想解在高概率下对不安全区域访问为零。在重新整理的 DSRL 基准上评测，并在由人类遥操作示范直接训练的真实移动机器人导航任务上验证，显著优于基线，且对数据稀缺与质量退化保持稳健。",
        "en": "DexDICE introduces dual-expert offline imitation learning, which uses two complementary data sources—safety-compliant but possibly suboptimal demonstrations, and high-return demonstrations that may violate safety guidelines—to obtain high returns with safety guarantees without hand-designed cost functions or a single expert that is both safe and optimal. It combines DICE-style offline learning with safe support constraints instead of conventional distribution constraints, and proves that the ideal solution has zero unsafe-region visitation with high probability. It is evaluated on a re-curated DSRL benchmark and on a real mobile-robot navigation task trained directly from human teleoperation, substantially outperforming baselines and remaining robust to data scarcity and quality degradation.",
    },
    "2611.09279": {
        "zh": "异常检测无需预定义异常类别，但让安全人员理解每次判定的依据，才能评估该判定是否可信。端到端检测器准确率高却只输出标量分数；已有的异常声分离方法能给出可听的解释，检出精度却有限。AnomSep 先用以目标环境正常声学得的字典做基于优化的分离，得到正常声与异常声的初步估计；再用预训练音频隐空间上的深度神经网络精化该估计。分离出的异常声本身就是可听的解释，其能量决定异常分数。在合成与真实混合音频上，分离质量优于基线分离器，检测性能与端到端基线相当，同时为每个判定提供直接对应的可听依据。",
        "en": "AnomSep combines optimisation-based separation with deep neural refinement to deliver accurate anomaly detection together with listenable explanations. A dictionary learned from normal sounds in the target environment yields preliminary normal and anomalous sound estimates through optimisation-based separation, which a deep network then refines in a pretrained audio latent space; the separated anomalous sound is the listenable explanation and its energy determines the anomaly score. On synthetic and real mixtures it improves separation quality over baseline separators and achieves detection performance competitive with an end-to-end baseline, while giving an explanation directly tied to each decision.",
    },
    "2611.08914": {
        "zh": "VLM 驱动的家用机器人将进入已有摄像头、IoT 设备与佩戴可穿戴设备的居民住宅，必须与既有智能基础设施协同，并对歧义场景做出判断：烟雾报警可能来自即将起火的锅、已经着火的锅、正在做饭的居民，或一个故障传感器，每种都需要不同响应。HomeLoop 是基于 Isaac Sim 的仿真框架与基准，整合机器人本体、联网设备与可穿戴设备、模拟居民与访客、故障传感器以及随时间演化的危险；20 个任务分属五族，均取材于真实家庭危险与需求，并刻意让同一警报可有不同成因。运行时监视器用时序逻辑检查最终结果与过程中的动作，每个动作带预定义代价。评测六个开源与商用 VLM，最佳者族平衡得分 61.9%，并呈现普遍的「过度反应」：涉及禁止干预的失败集比漏掉必要干预的多两倍以上，模型常未查明原因就关掉炉子。",
        "en": "HomeLoop is an Isaac Sim-based simulation framework and benchmark for robot-IoT coordination in the home, combining robot bodies, networked devices and wearables, simulated residents and visitors, faulty sensors and hazards that evolve over time. Its 20 tasks across five families are grounded in real household hazards and are designed so that the same alert can have different causes; a runtime monitor scores each episode with temporal-logic checks on the outcome and on the actions taken, each carrying a predefined cost. Across six open-weight and proprietary VLMs the best reaches a family-balanced score of 61.9%, and failures involving prohibited interventions outnumber missed required interventions by more than two to one—models often shut off the stove before investigating the alarm's cause.",
    },
    "2611.09315": {
        "zh": "设计无漏洞的密码协议极为困难，广泛使用的协议中已出现大量设计缺陷与实现错误。近期工作用模型检验生成含 Dolev-Yao 攻击者行为的负向测试用例，但如何分析这类用例在协议实现上产生的执行轨迹仍是问题。作者提出用模型检验执行轨迹来检测安全属性违规：所用模型检验器基于带冻结算子的线性时序逻辑 DLTL，并配以前处理与后处理实现测试自动化——前者弥合不同抽象层次之间的落差，后者综合模型检验器的输出。文中给出实验结果，作为该方法可行性的概念验证。",
        "en": "Testing protocol implementations with negative test cases that embed Dolev-Yao attacker behaviour produces execution traces whose analysis is itself an open problem. The paper proposes detecting violations of security properties by model checking those traces, using a model checker based on DLTL, a linear temporal logic with freeze operators, and automating the testing process through pre- and post-processing steps that respectively bridge different levels of abstraction and synthesise the model checker's results. Experimental results serve as a proof of concept for feasibility.",
    },
    "2611.09048": {
        "zh": "LeanDojo-v2 是在 Lean 中做机器学习辅助定理证明的端到端框架，把仓库数据抽取、LLM 微调、证明搜索、AI 自动补全与 LLM 辅助证明统一到一个软件库中。配套的 Lean4Code 是轻量 IDE，用数学家友好的界面把这些能力整合起来。作者希望借此让数学家和研究者无需复杂配置，就能在领域专属的 Lean 代码库上微调语言模型、试验 LLM 辅助定理证明。",
        "en": "LeanDojo-v2 is an end-to-end framework that unifies repository data extraction, LLM fine-tuning, proof search, AI autocompletion and LLM-assisted theorem proving in Lean within a single software library, accompanied by Lean4Code, a lightweight IDE that exposes these features through a mathematician-friendly UI. The goal is to let mathematicians and researchers fine-tune language models on domain-specific Lean codebases and experiment with LLM-assisted proving without a complex setup.",
    },
    "2611.08711": {
        "zh": "黑盒场景下梯度不可得，已有对抗攻击方法多靠外部知识猜测变换，忽略了目标模型自身提供的信息。RL-ATTACK 提出可训练的黑盒框架，用强化学习从目标模型学习、生成针对性的对抗变换。在自然语言推断与生成式问答两类任务上，该方法攻击后准确率更低、查询更省、语义保持更好：自然语言推断上 20 次查询内即把攻击后准确率压到 2%；对生成式语言模型，训练过的攻击者稳定优于未训练者，与强优化基线相比 6 个设置中赢 4 个。作者还试验了多种奖励设计与训练设置，未发现有一致占优的方案。",
        "en": "RL-ATTACK is a trainable black-box adversarial attack framework that learns from the target model, via reinforcement learning, to generate tailored adversarial transformations, rather than guessing transformations from external knowledge as prior black-box methods do. It achieves lower post-attack accuracy, better query efficiency and stronger semantic preservation on natural language inference and generative question answering: on NLI it drives post-attack accuracy to 2% within 20 queries, and against generative models the trained attacker consistently beats the untrained one and wins 4 of 6 settings against a strong optimisation-based baseline. No reward design or training setting proved consistently dominant.",
    },
    "2611.09472": {
        "zh": "智能体通过外部检索与参数学习利用经验，而把经验固化进权重须同时决定「用哪些经验训练」与「何时可以让外部记录离开检索」。仅按学生掌握度准入会排除有用的教师示范，训练后立即删除又会丢弃模型仍需要的指引。ENGRAM 把训练准入与记忆释放分离：示范感知的准入闸门按学生掌握度或足够多次成功教师示范接纳技能，学生借助 Engram Trace Graph 提供的上下文从选定动作轨迹学习；随后验证闸门在保留探针上比较「无情景检索的更新模型」与「带检索的基座模型」，只有在训练确实参与且相对与绝对指标同时达标时才释放记录，未通过者仍可检索。在交互与推理基准上稳定优于冻结权重的 ETG 对照，受控留出对比显示经验证的释放大幅缩减可检索足迹，性能接近「全部保留」并优于立即释放与等预算随机释放，同时减少输入 token 与模型调用。",
        "en": "ENGRAM separates training admission from memory release when consolidating agent experience into model weights. A demonstration-aware gate admits skills based on student mastery or sufficient successful teacher demonstrations, the student learns from selected action traces with context from an Engram Trace Graph, and a verification gate then compares the updated model without episodic retrieval against the base model with retrieval on reserved probes; release requires valid training participation plus relative and absolute criteria, and records failing verification stay retrievable. Experiments show consistent gains over frozen-weight ETG controls, and a controlled held-out comparison shows verified release substantially shrinks the retrievable footprint while staying close to retain-all performance and beating immediate and budget-matched random release, with lower input-token usage and fewer model calls.",
    },
    "2611.08779": {
        "zh": "持久记忆系统不仅决定检索哪些记录，还决定哪些先验信息可以改变当前推理。JCMC 用「预测影响签名」在共享的行为度量空间中表示每一次被授权的记忆干预，按目标效应与副作用预算选择干预，并在保留或回滚前比较预测效应与实际观测效应。在显式光滑性与有界估计假设下，作者证明二次局部近似界，刻画一组签名可达到的目标效应集合，给出签名误差下的选择遗憾界，并界定多条记忆同时作用时的非可加交互。需要指出：本文不含基准实测，只定义了配对反事实估计量与评测协议，用以把 JCMC 与基于相关性、图结构、策略过滤的检索基线对比；若这些更简单的基线在同等模型、记忆、策略与成本预算下也能做到效应定向、副作用控制与回滚效用，本文的核心主张即被削弱或证伪。",
        "en": "Jacobian-causal memory control (JCMC) represents each authorised memory intervention by a predicted influence signature in a shared behavioural measurement space, selects interventions against a target effect and side-effect budget, and compares predicted with observed effects before retaining or rolling back. Under explicit smoothness and bounded-estimation assumptions it proves a quadratic local-approximation bound, characterises the reachable target effects, bounds selection regret under signature error, and bounds non-additive interactions between simultaneous memories. Notably, the paper reports no benchmark measurements: it defines a paired counterfactual estimator and an evaluation protocol against relevance, graph and policy-filtered retrieval baselines, and states that the central claim is narrowed or falsified if those simpler baselines match effect targeting, side-effect control and rollback utility under equal budgets.",
    },
    "2611.09736": {
        "zh": "2026 年 7 月 OpenAI 的智能体攻破 Hugging Face，同年 10 月同一公司发布七百多篇 AI 生成的数学证明手稿；前者被读作安全失败，后者被读作数学成功。作者用其混合框架（Kim & Kang, 2026）统一解读：编码、证明与从数据中学习都是同一演绎机制的推导，区别只在前提的种类。两起事件背后是同一个循环——统计提议者产生候选漏洞或证明，演绎验证者用一次推导判定每一个。真正分隔二者的是两个领域所需命题的逻辑形式：程序安全是 Π1 命题（不存在漏洞），有限次通过测试无法保证；可证明性是 Σ1 命题（存在证明），单个被验证者检验过的证明即可保证。其背后是图灵不可判定性定理：停机集是 Σ1 但不可判定，其补集是 Π1 而非 Σ1，即成员资格有有限见证、非成员资格没有。作者证明，无论提议者多强，把统计提议者接到演绎验证者上都不改变这一不可判定性结论，并讨论真正能保证安全的是什么、残余风险去了哪里。",
        "en": "Reading two 2026 events—OpenAI agents breaching Hugging Face and the same company releasing over seven hundred AI-generated proof manuscripts—through a hybrid framework in which coding, proving and learning are derivations by one deductive mechanism distinguished by premise kinds. Both events run the same loop: a statistical proposer emits candidate exploits or proofs and a deductive verifier settles each by a derivation. What separates them is logical form: safety is a Π1 statement (no exploit exists), not assured by any finite list of passed tests, whereas provability is Σ1 (a proof exists), assured by a single checked instance. The underlying theorem is Turing's undecidability result—the halting set is Σ1 but undecidable, so its complement is Π1 and not Σ1. The authors prove that attaching a statistical proposer to a deductive verifier does not change this, however good the proposer, and discuss what does assure safety and where residual risk goes.",
    },
    "2611.08971": {
        "zh": "多智能体 LLM 系统常聚合多个模型实例的判断，但「推理其他智能体」本身会引入失效。作者研究这样一种情形：LLM 在观察到含糊的社会信号后改变公开决策，同时对他者私下判断给出不准确的估计，即使群体记录的私下判断并不支持那个看似达成的共识。作者称之为「幻影共识」，并作为受控 LLM 群体中的多元无知式模式来研究，构建 PHANTOM-Bench 把五个环节分开测量：孤立私下判断、含糊社会信号后的公开决策、对群体私下判断的估计、基于透明度的恢复，以及中性公开文本与显式服从多数的对照。九个开源与闭源模型上，含糊公开信号一致地损害决策质量，可把正确的私下群体判断扭成错误的公开集体结果，公开准确率最多下降 47.8 个百分点，最易受影响设置下集体理性失效率达 47.3%；公开阶段失效同时伴随对群体私下信念的显著误估；仅公开各智能体记录的私下决策即可修复多数失效而不泄露金标签，但恢复程度因模型而异。",
        "en": "Phantom consensus names a pluralistic-ignorance-style failure in LLM collectives where models shift public decisions after ambiguous social signals while misreporting what others privately judged, even when recorded private judgments do not support the apparent consensus. PHANTOM-Bench separates isolated private judgments, public decisions after ambiguous signals, elicited estimates of group-private judgment, transparency-based recovery, and controls for neutral text and explicit vote-following. Across nine closed- and open-weight models, ambiguous public signals consistently degrade decision quality and can turn correct private group judgments into incorrect public outcomes—public accuracy drops by as much as 47.8 percentage points and collective rationality failures reach 47.3% in the most susceptible setting—with substantial misestimation of group-private beliefs. Revealing recorded private decisions repairs many failures without revealing the gold label, though recovery varies by model.",
    },
}


def main():
    path = os.path.join(OUT, "summaries.json")
    cur = json.load(open(path, encoding="utf-8"))
    before = len(cur)
    added = updated = 0
    for sid, v in SUMM.items():
        old = cur.get(sid)
        if isinstance(old, dict) and old.get("zh") and old.get("en"):
            continue
        cur[sid] = {"en": v["en"], "zh": v["zh"]}
        if old is None:
            added += 1
        else:
            updated += 1
    json.dump(cur, open(path, "w", encoding="utf-8"), ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)
    print("summaries.json %d -> %d (added %d, updated %d)" % (before, len(cur), added, updated))


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
